        {
          "id": "intro",
          "type": "text",
          "role": "content",
          "text": "*Most busy mornings go wrong in the same few places.*\n\n- The evening ran late.\n- Something went missing.\n- There were too many decisions before breakfast.",
          "size": 14.7,
          "lineHeight": 19.2,
          "listLineHeight": 17.64,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "highlight",
          "type": "highlight",
          "role": "content",
          "text": "The fix that works most often:\nmake one decision the night before.",
          "size": 17.3,
          "lineHeight": 24.65,
          "gap": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "article",
          "type": "text",
          "role": "content",
          "text": "***Three things to try tonight.***\n\n1. **Set out tomorrow's clothes.** Two minutes now saves ten later.\n2. **Put the bag by the door.** Nothing to hunt for on the way out.\n3. **Decide on breakfast.** One question fewer when everyone is hungry.\n\nYou don't need a new routine. One early decision is usually enough.",
          "size": 14.7,
          "lineHeight": 19.2,
          "listLineHeight": 17.64,
          "align": "left"
        }
